2026-09-25 19:17:00,613 | hr_assistant.pipeline | INFO | Final answer: **How to avail leave**

1. **Check your entitlement**  
   * Full‑time employees have **20 paid annual leave days** per calendar year.  
   * You also have **10 paid sick days** per year (separate from annual leave).

2. **Submit a leave request**  
   * Log in to the **HR portal**.  
   * Choose the appropriate leave type (annual, sick, etc.).  
   * Enter the start and end dates and any required notes.  
   * **Submit at least 5 working days before the first day of leave** (except for emergency sick leave).

3. **Manager approval**  
   * Your manager will review the request and either approve or request changes.  
   * You will receive a notification of the decision in the portal.

4. **Special cases**  
   * **Sick leave > 2 consecutive days** – attach a medical certificate to the portal request.  
   * **During probation (first 3 months)** – paid leave is not available; you may request **unpaid leave** for emergencies, subject to manager approval.

5. **Leave balance & carry‑forward**  
   * Unused annual leave can be carried forward **up to 5 days** into the next calendar year.  
   * Check your remaining balance in the HR portal before submitting a request.

6. **After approval**  
   * The system will update your leave balance automatically.  
   * Ensure any work hand‑over or coverage is arranged with your team before you are away.

If you need help navigating the HR portal or have any other questions, feel free to ask!
